  "source": "JoyPro curated on the maker's photo (2026-10-11), seen from the pilot side front-left and above: button panel nearest the camera (lower right), speed brake handle on the left lever slot, the two thrust levers with their joined white handles at the top",
  "mappingSource": "TCA Quadrant Boeing Edition user manual (https://ts.thrustmaster.com/download/accessories/Manuals/TCA_Quadrant_Boeing/TCA_Quadrant_Boeing_Edition_user_manual.pdf) p.5 \"Mapping for the 17 buttons and 3 axes on PC\": levers Xr/Yr/Zr left to right, 1-3 main lever handles, 4-6 the small (reverser) handles, panel row 7/8/9 next to the levers, 10 and 11 the lower row, 12-14 the outer selector ring (IAS/MACH, HDG/TRK, ALTITUDE), 15/16 rotate, 17 push of the SEL knob; cross-checked with https://ts.thrustmaster.com/download/pictures/Mappings/MappingTCAyokePack_PC.PDF p.2",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "note": "This photo has the speed brake handle fitted on lever 1 (the manual figure shows three thrust handles); whether lever 1 then still reports buttons 1/4 is not documented, so they are candidates only. Buttons 1-6 sit on the lever handles; the manual figure points at the handles, not at a distinct button face, so the markers sit on the handles. The reverser handles 4-6 are not clearly identifiable on this angle. The engine selector 1&2 / 3&4 (manual feature 5) changes the device name only, not the numbering.",
